      "id": 1,
      "text": "Halls Crossing was established in 1882 by a pioneer who ran a ferry crossing over the Colorado River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/hallscrossinghistory.shtml"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The founder of Halls Crossing also developed the specific boats used for ferrying people across the Colorado River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/hallscrossinghistory.shtml"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "State Route 276 crosses the Colorado River at Halls Crossing using the Charles Hall Ferry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halls_Crossing%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A small settlement existed at Halls Crossing from 1881 to 1883 before it quickly faded away.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/hallscrossinghistory.shtml"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Halls Crossing developed on the east side of Lake Powell after the dam was built and the river filled in.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/hallscrossinghistory.shtml"
    },
    {
